body:
Potentially broken in https://github.com/okta/terraform-provider-okta/issues/1855 / https://github.com/okta/terraform-provider-okta/pull/2008 - when we update the `okta_brand` resource, it seems that the provider is a little too aggressive at setting the fields in the update brand request function. It includes fields that are optional, and potentially unset.

Unfortunately when setting the fields from the model, even if the field is unset coming back from the API representation, it ends up being set to the zero value instead and thus we over-eagerly update fields. The provider should only set fields we are telling it to, or preserve existing non-null values set automatically by the API.

We see this in the Terraform plan:

```
  # module.okta_core.module.okta_tenant_xxxx.okta_brand.this will be updated in-place
  ~ resource "okta_brand" "this" {
      ~ agree_to_custom_privacy_policy = false -> (known after apply)
      ~ brand_id                       = "xxxx" -> (known after apply)
      + custom_privacy_policy_url      = (known after apply)
      + default_app_app_instance_id    = "xxxx"
      + default_app_app_link_name      = "xxxx"
      ~ email_domain_id                = "xxxx" -> (known after apply)
        id                             = "xxxx"
      ~ is_default                     = false -> (known after apply)
      ~ links                          = jsonencode(
            {
              - emailDomain = {
                  - hints = {
                      - allow = [
                          - "GET",
                          - "PUT",
                        ]
                    }
                  - href  = "https://xxxx.oktapreview.com/api/v1/email-domains/xxxx"
                }
              - self        = {
                  - hints = {
                      - allow = [
                          - "GET",
                          - "PUT",
                          - "DELETE",
                        ]
                    }
                  - href  = "https://xxxx.oktapreview.com/api/v1/brands/xxxx"
                }
              - themes      = {
                  - hints = {
                      - allow = [
                          - "GET",
                        ]
                    }
                  - href  = "https://xxxx.oktapreview.com/api/v1/brands/xxxx/themes"
                }
            }
        ) -> (known after apply)
        name                           = "xxx"
        # (1 unchanged attribute hidden)
    }
```
